<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title>firewall change</title>
  <style>
    body { color:#202124;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:1.55;margin:32px;max-width:900px; }
    h1, h2 { color:#1f2933; }
    h1 { border-bottom:2px solid #d8dee4;padding-bottom:8px; }
    li { margin:6px 0; }
    table { border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin:14px 0; }
    th, td { border:1px solid #999;padding:8px;text-align:left; }
    th { background:#f1f5f9; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Firewall Change Standard Operating Procedure (SOP)</h1>
<p>This SOP outlines the steps for updating the firewall configuration in ServiceNow.</p>

<h2>Purpose</h2>
<p>The purpose of this SOP is to ensure a secure and efficient update of the firewall configuration, minimizing downtime and potential security risks.</p>

<h2>Scope</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Applicable to all IT staff with access to ServiceNow</li>
  <li>Scope includes updating firewall rules and configurations</li>
</ul>

<h2>Prerequisites</h2>
<ol>
  <li>ServiceNow administrator account with necessary permissions</li>
  <li>Familiarity with ServiceNow firewall configuration</li>
</ol>

<h2>Roles and Responsibilities</h2>
<table border="1" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0">
  <thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Responsibility</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody><tr><td>IT Administrator</td><td>Update firewall rules and configurations</td></tr><tr><td>ServiceNow User</td><td>Verify firewall changes have been applied successfully</td></tr></tbody>
</table>

<h2>Procedure</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Create a backup of the current firewall configuration using ServiceNow's built-in backup tool.</li>
  <li>Login to ServiceNow as an administrator and navigate to the Firewall Configuration page.</li>
  <li>Select the rules to be updated or added, and enter the new configuration values in the required fields.</li>
  <li>Click the "Save" button to apply the changes.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Required Screenshot / Image</h2>
<div style="border:1px solid #999;padding:16px;background:#f5f5f5;">
  <strong>Image Placeholder:</strong> The generated image will be inserted here after ServiceNow attachment upload.
</div>

<h2>Validation</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Verify the updated firewall rules and configurations are correct by comparing them to the backup created earlier.</li>
  <li>Test network connectivity to ensure all affected systems can access resources as expected.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
<table border="1" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0">
  <thead><tr><th>Issue</th><th>Cause</th><th>Resolution</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody><tr><td>The firewall rules are not being applied.</td><td>Cause: Insufficient permissions or incorrect configuration values.</td><td>Resolution: Check and update permissions, or review and correct the configuration values.</td></tr><tr><td>No network connectivity is available.</td><td>Cause: Incorrect firewall rule settings.</td><td>Resolution: Review and adjust the affected firewall rules to ensure proper network connectivity.</td></tr></tbody>
</table>

<h2>Rollback / Recovery</h2>
<ol>
  <li>In case of an error or unexpected change, log out of ServiceNow immediately and restart the system to revert changes.</li>
  <li>If a backup is created during the update process, restore from the backup to revert changes.</li>
</ol>

<h2>References</h2>
<ul>
  <li>ServiceNow Firewall Configuration Guide</li>
  <li>IT Service Management Best Practices</li>
</ul>
</body>
</html>
